/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Matthew chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("matthew", [
{n:1, name:"The Genealogy of Christ", seal:{ref:"Matthew 1:21",verse:"And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name JESUS: for he shall save his people from their sins."}, facts:["Did you know Matthew's genealogy names five women, Thamar, Rachab, Ruth, the wife of Urias, and Mary? Women almost never appeared in ancient genealogies, yet God wove them into His Son's line.","Did you know Matthew arranges the genealogy in three sets of fourteen generations, from Abraham to David, David to the Babylonian exile, and the exile to Christ? It is a deliberately ordered history, not a random list.","Did you know the angel told Joseph the child's name before He was born, and explained it? Jesus means Saviour, for He shall save His people from their sins (Matthew 1:21)."], questions:[
{q:"Whose book of generation opens Matthew's Gospel?", options:["Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham","John the Baptist, the son of Zacharias","Simon Peter, the son of Jonas","Paul the apostle, the servant of Christ"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:1",verse:"The book of the generation of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham.", insight:"The first verse names Him by His two great titles at once, Messiah and promised King. Matthew wants you to know who this is before anything else."},
{q:"Who begat Isaac, according to the genealogy?", options:["Abraham","Jacob","Isaac begat himself of his own house","Jesse"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:2",verse:"Abraham begat Isaac; and Isaac begat Jacob; and Jacob begat Judas and his brethren;", insight:"Abraham begins the line, the father of promise. Every name after him is a link in God's long keeping of His word."},
{q:"Which woman is named as the mother of Phares and Zara?", options:["Thamar","Rachab","Ruth","Mary"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:3",verse:"And Judas begat Phares and Zara of Thamar; and Phares begat Esrom; and Esrom begat Aram;", insight:"Thamar's story is tangled and uncomfortable, yet there she is in Christ's line. Grace does not wait for a spotless family tree."},
{q:"Who was the mother of Obed?", options:["Ruth","Rachab","Thamar","Mary"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:5",verse:"And Salmon begat Booz of Rachab; and Booz begat Obed of Ruth; and Obed begat Jesse;", insight:"Ruth was a Moabitess, an outsider welcomed in. From the start, God's family was bigger than one nation."},
{q:"Which king is named by title in the genealogy?", options:["David the king","Solomon the king","Hezekiah the king","Josiah the king"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:6",verse:"And Jesse begat David the king; and David the king begat Solomon of her that had been the wife of Urias;", insight:"David the king. The promise of an everlasting throne runs through him straight to Jesus."},
{q:"About what time was Jechonias begat?", options:["About the time they were carried away to Babylon","About the time David took the throne","About the time Solomon built the temple","About the time Israel left Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:11",verse:"And Josias begat Jechonias and his brethren, about the time they were carried away to Babylon:", insight:"The exile was Israel's darkest chapter, and Matthew names it plainly. God's plan survived even the captivity."},
{q:"Who was the son of Jacob, the last named father in the genealogy?", options:["Joseph the husband of Mary","Joseph the son of Rachel","Joseph the dreamer of Egypt","Joseph the carpenter of Nazareth, a different Joseph"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:16",verse:"And Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who is called Christ.", insight:"Joseph the husband of Mary. Matthew is careful: Joseph is the legal father, but the child is born of Mary alone."},
{q:"How many generations make up each section of the genealogy?", options:["Fourteen generations","Twelve generations","Ten generations","Seven generations"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:17",verse:"So all the generations from Abraham to David are fourteen generations; and from David until the carrying away into Babylon are fourteen generations; and from the carrying away into Babylon unto Christ are fourteen generations.", insight:"Fourteen, fourteen, fourteen. The careful counting shows a God who orders history, not one who drifts through it."},
{q:"Before Joseph and Mary came together, how was Mary found?", options:["With child of the Holy Ghost","With child by another man","Betrothed to a second husband","Sent away from Nazareth"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:18",verse:"Now the birth of Jesus Christ was on this wise: When as his mother Mary was espoused to Joseph, before they came together, she was found with child of the Holy Ghost.", insight:"With child of the Holy Ghost. The birth of Jesus is God's doing from the very first moment."},
{q:"Joseph is called a just man. What was he minded to do about Mary?", options:["To put her away privily","To make her a public example","To accuse her before the priests","To flee into Egypt at once"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:19",verse:"Then Joseph her husband, being a just man, and not willing to make her a publick example, was minded to put her away privily.", insight:"He was just and also kind. He wanted to protect her even while he believed the worst, a mercy worth imitating."},
{q:"How did the angel of the Lord appear to Joseph?", options:["In a dream","In the temple at Jerusalem","At the well of Nazareth","In a pillar of fire"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:20",verse:"But while he thought on these things, behold, the angel of the Lord appeared unto him in a dream, saying, Joseph, thou son of David, fear not to take unto thee Mary thy wife: for that which is conceived in her is of the Holy Ghost.", insight:"In a dream. God spoke to Joseph in the quiet of sleep, and Joseph woke up and obeyed without arguing."},
{q:"What did the angel tell Joseph to call the son?", options:["JESUS, for He shall save His people from their sins","Emmanuel, for God is with us","Christ, for He is the anointed","Nazarene, for He shall dwell in Nazareth"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:21",verse:"And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name JESUS: for he shall save his people from their sins.", insight:"Jesus, because He saves. His name is His mission, and His mission is rescue."},
{q:"What does the name Emmanuel mean?", options:["God with us","God saves His people","Prince of peace","Mighty God"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:23",verse:"Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, God with us.", insight:"God with us. The whole Gospel in two words: He did not stay distant, He came near."},
{q:"What did Joseph do when he was raised from sleep?", options:["He did as the angel had bidden him, and took unto him his wife","He waited for a second dream","He asked the priests for counsel","He wrote down the dream and kept it"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:24",verse:"Then Joseph being raised from sleep did as the angel of the Lord had bidden him, and took unto him his wife:", insight:"He simply obeyed. Joseph is the Bible's great example of quiet, immediate obedience."},
{q:"What did Joseph call his firstborn son?", options:["JESUS","Emmanuel","Joseph after himself","David after his ancestor"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:25",verse:"And knew her not till she had brought forth her firstborn son: and he called his name JESUS.", insight:"He called His name Jesus, exactly as the angel said. Obedience often looks like doing the plain thing you were told."},
{q:"Of whom was it said that Jesus was born?", options:["Of Mary, the wife of Joseph","Of Thamar the Canaanite","Of Rachab of Jericho","Of Ruth the Moabitess"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:16",verse:"And Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who is called Christ.", insight:"Of whom, Mary, was born Jesus. Matthew bends the whole genealogy toward one woman and her Son."},
{q:"Into how many sets of fourteen generations is the genealogy divided?", options:["Three sets","Two sets","Four sets","One unbroken list"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:17",verse:"So all the generations from Abraham to David are fourteen generations; and from David until the carrying away into Babylon are fourteen generations; and from the carrying away into Babylon unto Christ are fourteen generations.", insight:"Three sets of fourteen, from Abraham to David, David to the exile, the exile to Christ. History with a shape, moving toward Jesus."},
{q:"Which two Gentile women appear in verse 5 of the genealogy?", options:["Rachab and Ruth","Thamar and Rachab","Ruth and Mary","Thamar and the wife of Urias"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:5",verse:"And Salmon begat Booz of Rachab; and Booz begat Obed of Ruth; and Obed begat Jesse;", insight:"Rachab and Ruth, both outsiders. The Saviour's family tree has room for the foreigner from the very start."},
{q:"Whose brethren are mentioned alongside Judas in verse 2?", options:["Judas and his brethren, the sons of Jacob","Judas and his brethren, the apostles","Judas Iscariot and his followers","Judas and his brethren of Nazareth"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:2",verse:"Abraham begat Isaac; and Isaac begat Jacob; and Jacob begat Judas and his brethren;", insight:"Judas and his brethren, the twelve sons of Jacob. One verse holds the seed of the whole nation of Israel."},
{q:"What did the angel call Joseph when he appeared to him?", options:["Joseph, thou son of David","Joseph of Nazareth, carpenter","Joseph, husband of Mary","Joseph, keeper of the child"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 1:20",verse:"But while he thought on these things, behold, the angel of the Lord appeared unto him in a dream, saying, Joseph, thou son of David, fear not to take unto thee Mary thy wife: for that which is conceived in her is of the Holy Ghost.", insight:"Thou son of David. The angel reminded Joseph who he was, a son of the kingly line, before asking him to trust God."}
]},
{n:2, name:"The Visit of the Wise Men", seal:{ref:"Matthew 2:11",verse:"And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh."}, facts:["Did you know Matthew never says there were three wise men, and never calls them kings? The number three comes from the three gifts: gold, frankincense, and myrrh.","Did you know Herod killed the children two years old and under, based on when the star appeared? That suggests Jesus may have been as old as two when the wise men arrived, not a newborn in the manger.","Did you know Matthew ties these events to three old prophecies? Bethlehem from Micah, Out of Egypt from Hosea, and Rachel weeping from Jeremiah. The whole chapter is fulfillment."], questions:[
{q:"Where was Jesus born, and in whose days?", options:["In Bethlehem of Judaea, in the days of Herod the king","In Nazareth of Galilee, in the days of Caesar","In Jerusalem, in the days of Archelaus","In Bethlehem of Galilee, in the days of Pilate"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:1",verse:"Now when Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judaea in the days of Herod the king, behold, there came wise men from the east to Jerusalem,", insight:"Bethlehem of Judaea, under Herod. The King of the Jews was born while a violent pretender sat on the throne."},
{q:"Who came from the east to Jerusalem?", options:["Wise men","Shepherds from the fields","Merchants of Arabia","Priests from Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:1",verse:"Now when Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judaea in the days of Herod the king, behold, there came wise men from the east to Jerusalem,", insight:"Wise men from the east. Gentile seekers noticed the star before Jerusalem's own scholars noticed the Scriptures."},
{q:"What question did the wise men ask in Jerusalem?", options:["Where is he that is born King of the Jews?","Where is the prophet promised by Moses?","Where shall we find the temple of God?","Where is Herod the king?"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:2",verse:"Saying, Where is he that is born King of the Jews? for we have seen his star in the east, and are come to worship him.", insight:"Where is He that is born King of the Jews? They had seen His star and come to worship, the right question and the right reason."},
{q:"How did Herod react to the wise men's news?", options:["He was troubled, and all Jerusalem with him","He rejoiced and ordered a feast","He sent gifts to Bethlehem","He ignored them and went to Rome"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:3",verse:"When Herod the king had heard these things, he was troubled, and all Jerusalem with him.", insight:"He was troubled, and all Jerusalem with him. A guilty conscience hears good news as a threat."},
{q:"Whom did Herod gather to ask where Christ should be born?", options:["All the chief priests and scribes of the people","The Roman governors of Judaea","The elders of Bethlehem","The captains of his guard"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:4",verse:"And when he had gathered all the chief priests and scribes of the people together, he demanded of them where Christ should be born.", insight:"The chief priests and scribes knew the answer from Scripture but never went to see. Knowing the Bible is not the same as following it."},
{q:"Where did the chief priests and scribes say Christ should be born?", options:["In Bethlehem of Judaea","In Nazareth of Galilee","In Jerusalem the holy city","In Egypt by the Nile"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:5",verse:"And they said unto him, In Bethlehem of Judaea: for thus it is written by the prophet,", insight:"In Bethlehem of Judaea, for thus it is written by the prophet. The scholars had the right verse; they just lacked the wise men's feet."},
{q:"According to the prophecy quoted, who would come out of Bethlehem?", options:["A Governor, that shall rule my people Israel","A priest, that shall serve in the temple","A prophet, that shall speak to the nations","A judge, that shall deliver Judaea"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:6",verse:"And thou Bethlehem, in the land of Juda, art not the least among the princes of Juda: for out of thee shall come a Governor, that shall rule my people Israel.", insight:"A Governor that shall rule. Bethlehem was small, but the prophet said it was not the least. God loves small places."},
{q:"What did Herod diligently enquire of the wise men?", options:["What time the star appeared","How many men travelled with them","What road they took from the east","What gifts they carried"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:7",verse:"Then Herod, when he had privily called the wise men, enquired of them diligently what time the star appeared.", insight:"What time the star appeared. He asked in secret, already calculating murder. Beware the questions of the jealous."},
{q:"What did Herod tell the wise men to do when they found the child?", options:["Bring me word again, that I may come and worship him also","Stay in Bethlehem and guard him","Send him to Jerusalem to the temple","Take him to Egypt for safety"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:8",verse:"And he sent them to Bethlehem, and said, Go and search diligently for the young child; and when ye have found him, bring me word again, that I may come and worship him also.", insight:"He claimed he wanted to worship. Lies often wear the clothes of devotion."},
{q:"What did the star do when the wise men left Jerusalem?", options:["It went before them, till it stood over where the young child was","It faded into the morning sky","It fell to the earth in Bethlehem","It joined the other stars and vanished"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:9",verse:"When they had heard the king, they departed; and, lo, the star, which they saw in the east, went before them, till it came and stood over where the young child was.", insight:"It went before them and stood over the house. God guided them the last mile, not just the first."},
{q:"How did the wise men rejoice when they saw the star?", options:["With exceeding great joy","With quiet, solemn reverence","With fear and trembling","With singing and dancing"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:10",verse:"When they saw the star, they rejoiced with exceeding great joy.", insight:"With exceeding great joy. The journey was long and the danger real, but the sight of God's guidance made them glad."},
{q:"What three gifts did the wise men present to the child?", options:["Gold, and frankincense, and myrrh","Gold, silver, and precious stones","Myrrh, aloes, and spices","Bread, wine, and oil"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:11",verse:"And when they were come into the house, they saw the young child with Mary his mother, and fell down, and worshipped him: and when they had opened their treasures, they presented unto him gifts; gold, and frankincense, and myrrh.", insight:"Gold for a King, frankincense for God, myrrh for burial. Their gifts told His story before He could speak."},
{q:"How were the wise men warned not to return to Herod?", options:["Being warned of God in a dream","By a letter from the chief priests","By the star turning them back","By Roman soldiers on the road"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:12",verse:"And being warned of God in a dream that they should not return to Herod, they departed into their own country another way.", insight:"Warned of God in a dream. God protected the seekers who had sought Him honestly."},
{q:"Where did the angel tell Joseph to flee with the child?", options:["Into Egypt","Into the wilderness of Judaea","Across the Jordan to Perea","Back to Nazareth"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:13",verse:"And when they were departed, behold, the angel of the Lord appeareth to Joseph in a dream, saying, Arise, and take the young child and his mother, and flee into Egypt, and be thou there until I bring thee word: for Herod will seek the young child to destroy him.", insight:"Flee into Egypt. The Son of God began His life as a refugee, and God has never forgotten the displaced."},
{q:"At what time of day did Joseph depart for Egypt?", options:["By night","At sunrise","At noon","At the evening sacrifice"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:14",verse:"When he arose, he took the young child and his mother by night, and departed into Egypt:", insight:"By night. Joseph did not wait for morning. When God says go, the hour is always now."},
{q:"How long did the family stay in Egypt?", options:["Until the death of Herod","For forty days","For seven years","Until Jesus was twelve"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:15",verse:"And was there until the death of Herod: that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of the Lord by the prophet, saying, Out of Egypt have I called my son.", insight:"Until the death of Herod. God set the length of the exile; Joseph simply stayed until the word came to return."},
{q:"How old were the children Herod ordered slain in Bethlehem?", options:["From two years old and under","All under ten years","Only the newborn males","All under one year"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:16",verse:"Then Herod, when he saw that he was mocked of the wise men, was exceeding wroth, and sent forth, and slew all the children that were in Bethlehem, and in all the coasts thereof, from two years old and under, according to the time which he had diligently enquired of the wise men.", insight:"From two years old and under. Herod's cruelty was precise and cold, measured by the star's appearing."},
{q:"In what place was the voice of Rachel weeping heard?", options:["In Rama","In Bethlehem","In Jerusalem","In Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:18",verse:"In Rama was there a voice heard, lamentation, and weeping, and great mourning, Rachel weeping for her children, and would not be comforted, because they are not.", insight:"In Rama was heard lamentation. Matthew does not skip the grief; the Gospel holds both the joy of worship and the sorrow of loss."},
{q:"What did the angel tell Joseph after Herod died?", options:["Arise, and take the young child and his mother, and go into the land of Israel","Stay in Egypt, for Archelaus is worse","Go to Jerusalem and show the child","Flee to the parts of Syria"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:20",verse:"Saying, Arise, and take the young child and his mother, and go into the land of Israel: for they are dead which sought the young child’s life.", insight:"Go into the land of Israel, for they are dead which sought the young child's life. God's timing opens doors that fear had shut."},
{q:"Why did Joseph turn aside into Galilee instead of Judaea?", options:["He heard that Archelaus reigned in Judaea in his father Herod's place","The angel forbade him to enter Jerusalem","The wise men warned him in a letter","There was famine in Judaea"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 2:22",verse:"But when he heard that Archelaus did reign in Judaea in the room of his father Herod, he was afraid to go thither: notwithstanding, being warned of God in a dream, he turned aside into the parts of Galilee:", insight:"He was afraid because of Archelaus, and God confirmed the turn in a dream. Caution and guidance can walk together."}
]},
{n:3, name:"John the Baptist and the Baptism of Jesus", seal:{ref:"Matthew 3:17",verse:"And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased."}, facts:["Did you know John's clothing and diet matched Elijah's? Camel's hair and a leather girdle marked him as the promised forerunner, the Elijah who was to come.","Did you know John's sharpest words were for the religious leaders, not the crowds? 'Generation of vipers' was aimed at Pharisees and Sadducees who came without repentance.","Did you know all three persons of the Trinity appear at Jesus' baptism? The Son stands in the water, the Spirit descends like a dove, and the Father speaks from heaven."], questions:[
{q:"Where did John the Baptist preach?", options:["In the wilderness of Judaea","In the temple at Jerusalem","On the shores of Galilee","In the synagogues of Nazareth"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:1",verse:"In those days came John the Baptist, preaching in the wilderness of Judaea,", insight:"In the wilderness of Judaea. God often raises His voice far from the crowds, in the quiet places."},
{q:"What was the heart of John's preaching?", options:["Repent ye: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand","Believe and thou shalt be saved","The temple shall be rebuilt","The Romans shall be overthrown"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:2",verse:"And saying, Repent ye: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.", insight:"Repent, for the kingdom is at hand. Repentance is the doorway; you cannot enter the kingdom without turning around."},
{q:"Which prophet had spoken of John?", options:["Esaias","Jeremy","Ezekiel","Daniel"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:3",verse:"For this is he that was spoken of by the prophet Esaias, saying, The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make his paths straight.", insight:"Esaias, Isaiah, had named him centuries before: the voice crying in the wilderness. John's life was prophecy fulfilled."},
{q:"What did John wear?", options:["Raiment of camel's hair, and a leathern girdle about his loins","A priest's linen ephod","A soldier's cloak and sandals","Fine linen like a prince"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:4",verse:"And the same John had his raiment of camel’s hair, and a leathern girdle about his loins; and his meat was locusts and wild honey.", insight:"Camel's hair and a leather girdle. He dressed like Elijah because he carried Elijah's calling."},
{q:"What was John's food?", options:["Locusts and wild honey","Bread and fish from the lake","Figs and dates of the wilderness","Manna like Israel of old"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:4",verse:"And the same John had his raiment of camel’s hair, and a leathern girdle about his loins; and his meat was locusts and wild honey.", insight:"Locusts and wild honey. He lived simply so his message would be the rich thing, not his table."},
{q:"Who went out to hear John?", options:["Jerusalem, and all Judaea, and all the region round about Jordan","Only the poor of the wilderness","The Roman soldiers of Judaea","The priests of the temple alone"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:5",verse:"Then went out to him Jerusalem, and all Judaea, and all the region round about Jordan,", insight:"Jerusalem and all Judaea went out. When God moves, whole cities feel the pull toward the wilderness."},
{q:"Where were the people baptized by John?", options:["In Jordan, confessing their sins","In the pool of Siloam at Jerusalem","In the sea of Galilee","In the temple laver"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:6",verse:"And were baptized of him in Jordan, confessing their sins.", insight:"In Jordan, confessing their sins. The water meant nothing without the confession; honesty came first."},
{q:"What did John call the Pharisees and Sadducees who came?", options:["O generation of vipers","O children of Abraham","O beloved of the Lord","O seekers of truth"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:7",verse:"But when he saw many of the Pharisees and Sadducees come to his baptism, he said unto them, O generation of vipers, who hath warned you to flee from the wrath to come?", insight:"Generation of vipers. He saw through religious performance to the unrepentant heart beneath it."},
{q:"What did John demand as proof of repentance?", options:["Bring forth therefore fruits meet for repentance","Offer sacrifices at the temple","Memorize the words of the law","Follow him into the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:8",verse:"Bring forth therefore fruits meet for repentance:", insight:"Fruits meet for repentance. Real turning shows in changed living, not just wet robes."},
{q:"What did John say God could do with the stones?", options:["Raise up children unto Abraham from them","Build a new temple with them","Write the law upon them","Scatter them as a testimony"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:9",verse:"And think not to say within yourselves, We have Abraham to our father: for I say unto you, that God is able of these stones to raise up children unto Abraham.", insight:"God can raise up children unto Abraham from stones. No one is indispensable, and no one is beyond God's reach."},
{q:"What happens to the tree that brings not forth good fruit?", options:["It is hewn down, and cast into the fire","It is pruned and given more time","It is transplanted to better soil","It is left alone to grow wild"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:10",verse:"And now also the axe is laid unto the root of the trees: therefore every tree which bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire.", insight:"Hewn down and cast into the fire. Fruitlessness has an end date; now is the season to bear fruit."},
{q:"With what would the Mightier One baptize?", options:["With the Holy Ghost, and with fire","With water from the temple","With oil of anointing","With the dew of heaven"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:11",verse:"I indeed baptize you with water unto repentance: but he that cometh after me is mightier than I, whose shoes I am not worthy to bear: he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost, and with fire:", insight:"With the Holy Ghost and with fire. John's water prepared the way; Jesus would do the deeper work inside."},
{q:"What will the Mightier One do with the chaff?", options:["Burn it up with unquenchable fire","Scatter it to the wind","Feed it to the cattle","Plough it into the field"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:12",verse:"Whose fan is in his hand, and he will throughly purge his floor, and gather his wheat into the garner; but he will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire.", insight:"Burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire. The winnowing fan separates wheat from waste; judgment is thorough."},
{q:"Why did Jesus come from Galilee to Jordan?", options:["To be baptized of John","To hear John's preaching","To call His first disciples","To escape Herod's notice"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:13",verse:"Then cometh Jesus from Galilee to Jordan unto John, to be baptized of him.", insight:"To be baptized of John. The sinless One stepped into the waters of repentance to stand with sinners."},
{q:"Why did John forbid Jesus at first?", options:["I have need to be baptized of thee, and comest thou to me?","Thou art too young for baptism","The water is not deep enough here","The priests have forbidden it"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:14",verse:"But John forbad him, saying, I have need to be baptized of thee, and comest thou to me?", insight:"I have need to be baptized of thee. John knew the order was backwards; humility recognized its Master."},
{q:"What reason did Jesus give for being baptized?", options:["Thus it becometh us to fulfil all righteousness","To set an example for the crowds","To begin His ministry with a sign","To please His mother Mary"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:15",verse:"And Jesus answering said unto him, Suffer it to be so now: for thus it becometh us to fulfil all righteousness. Then he suffered him.", insight:"To fulfil all righteousness. Jesus did not skip one step of obedience, and neither should we."},
{q:"What descended like a dove when Jesus came up from the water?", options:["The Spirit of God","A cloud of glory","Fire from heaven","A white eagle"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:16",verse:"And Jesus, when he was baptized, went up straightway out of the water: and, lo, the heavens were opened unto him, and he saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove, and lighting upon him:", insight:"The Spirit of God, lighting upon Him. Heaven's approval rested visibly on the obedient Son."},
{q:"What did the voice from heaven say?", options:["This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased","This is the prophet promised by Moses","This is the king of Israel forever","This is my servant, hear ye him"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:17",verse:"And lo a voice from heaven, saying, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.", insight:"This is my beloved Son. Before Jesus preached one sermon, the Father declared His delight. Approval first, then work."},
{q:"In Isaiah's words, what was John's mission?", options:["Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make his paths straight","Build a new temple in the wilderness","Gather the tribes of Israel","Anoint the coming King with oil"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:3",verse:"For this is he that was spoken of by the prophet Esaias, saying, The voice of one crying in the wilderness, Prepare ye the way of the Lord, make his paths straight.", insight:"Prepare the way of the Lord. John was not the main road, he was the signpost pointing to it."},
{q:"What did John say about the shoes of the Mightier One?", options:["I am not worthy to bear them","They are shod with the gospel","They shall tread the winepress","They walk upon the waters"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 3:11",verse:"I indeed baptize you with water unto repentance: but he that cometh after me is mightier than I, whose shoes I am not worthy to bear: he shall baptize you with the Holy Ghost, and with fire:", insight:"Not worthy to bear His shoes. The greatest of prophets counted himself unfit for the lowest servant's task before Jesus."}
]},
{n:4, name:"The Temptation and the Calling", seal:{ref:"Matthew 4:19",verse:"And he saith unto them, Follow me, and I will make you fishers of men."}, facts:["Did you know Jesus answered every temptation with 'It is written'? All three replies come from Deuteronomy, the book Israel heard in the wilderness and failed to obey.","Did you know the forty days of fasting echo Israel's forty years in the wilderness? Where the nation stumbled, Jesus stood firm.","Did you know Capernaum became Jesus' home base for His ministry? Matthew later calls it 'his own city,' the town by the sea where so many miracles happened."], questions:[
{q:"Who led Jesus into the wilderness, and why?", options:["The Spirit led Him, to be tempted of the devil","The priests sent Him, to be tested","John sent Him, to pray alone","His mother urged Him, to rest"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:1",verse:"Then was Jesus led up of the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted of the devil.", insight:"The Spirit led Him to be tempted. Temptation is not always a sign you left God's path; sometimes God walks you straight into it."},
{q:"How long had Jesus fasted when the tempter came?", options:["Forty days and forty nights","Seven days and seven nights","Three days and three nights","Twelve days and twelve nights"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:2",verse:"And when he had fasted forty days and forty nights, he was afterward an hungred.", insight:"Forty days and forty nights. He was an hungred, fully human, yet He would not trade obedience for bread."},
{q:"What was the tempter's first challenge to Jesus?", options:["Command that these stones be made bread","Turn this water into wine","Call down manna from heaven","Feed the multitudes at once"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:3",verse:"And when the tempter came to him, he said, If thou be the Son of God, command that these stones be made bread.", insight:"Command these stones be made bread. The devil aimed at a real need, hunger, which is how temptation usually comes."},
{q:"How did Jesus answer the first temptation?", options:["Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God","Get thee hence, Satan","Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God","My meat is to do the will of Him that sent me"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:4",verse:"But he answered and said, It is written, Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceedeth out of the mouth of God.", insight:"Man shall not live by bread alone. God's word feeds deeper than bread; the soul has hungers the body cannot name."},
{q:"Where did the devil set Jesus for the second temptation?", options:["On a pinnacle of the temple in the holy city","On the Mount of Olives","On the roof of the synagogue","On the walls of Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:5",verse:"Then the devil taketh him up into the holy city, and setteth him on a pinnacle of the temple,", insight:"A pinnacle of the temple. The devil loves to tempt us in holy places, where we least expect him."},
{q:"What did the devil urge Jesus to do at the temple?", options:["Cast thyself down, for the angels will bear thee up","Leap across to the Mount of Olives","Call fire down upon the city","Preach to the priests below"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:6",verse:"And saith unto him, If thou be the Son of God, cast thyself down: for it is written, He shall give his angels charge concerning thee: and in their hands they shall bear thee up, lest at any time thou dash thy foot against a stone.", insight:"Cast thyself down. He even quoted Scripture, which proves the devil knows the Bible and still lies with it."},
{q:"How did Jesus answer the second temptation?", options:["It is written again, Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God","Man shall not live by bread alone","Get thee hence, Satan","Blessed are the pure in heart"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:7",verse:"Jesus said unto him, It is written again, Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God.", insight:"Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God. We do not test God to prove He is God; we trust Him because He is."},
{q:"Where did the devil take Jesus for the third temptation?", options:["Up into an exceeding high mountain","Into the holy of holies","To the top of Mount Sinai","To the wilderness of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:8",verse:"Again, the devil taketh him up into an exceeding high mountain, and sheweth him all the kingdoms of the world, and the glory of them;", insight:"An exceeding high mountain, showing all the kingdoms of the world. The view was real; the offer was a trap."},
{q:"What did the devil offer, and on what condition?", options:["All the kingdoms of the world, if Jesus would fall down and worship him","Bread for the hungry, if Jesus would leave Galilee","Riches beyond measure, if Jesus would keep silent","A throne in Jerusalem, if Jesus would deny the Father"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:9",verse:"And saith unto him, All these things will I give thee, if thou wilt fall down and worship me.", insight:"All these things will I give thee, if thou wilt worship me. Every shortcut to glory passes through worship of something lesser."},
{q:"What were Jesus' first words in answer to the third temptation?", options:["Get thee hence, Satan","It is written, Man shall not live by bread","Depart from me, tempter","Silence, deceiver"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:10",verse:"Then saith Jesus unto him, Get thee hence, Satan: for it is written, Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve.", insight:"Get thee hence, Satan. There comes a point where the answer is not debate but dismissal."},
{q:"What did Jesus say about whom we must worship?", options:["Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve","Worship the Father in Jerusalem only","Worship with the angels in heaven","Worship the God of thy fathers alone"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:10",verse:"Then saith Jesus unto him, Get thee hence, Satan: for it is written, Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve.", insight:"Him only shalt thou serve. Worship has no room for rivals; divided devotion is no devotion."},
{q:"What happened when the devil left Jesus?", options:["Angels came and ministered unto him","A great light shone around him","He slept under a juniper tree","He returned to Nazareth at once"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:11",verse:"Then the devil leaveth him, and, behold, angels came and ministered unto him.", insight:"Angels came and ministered unto Him. God never leaves the tested one empty; help comes after the battle."},
{q:"Why did Jesus depart into Galilee?", options:["He heard that John was cast into prison","Herod sought to kill Him","The feast was ended at Jerusalem","His mother called Him home"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:12",verse:"Now when Jesus had heard that John was cast into prison, he departed into Galilee;", insight:"When John was cast into prison, Jesus moved. One voice silenced, another rises; God's work does not stop with one man."},
{q:"In what city did Jesus come and dwell?", options:["Capernaum, upon the sea coast","Nazareth, where He was brought up","Bethlehem, where He was born","Jerusalem, the holy city"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:13",verse:"And leaving Nazareth, he came and dwelt in Capernaum, which is upon the sea coast, in the borders of Zabulon and Nephthalim:", insight:"Capernaum, upon the sea coast. He left Nazareth and made His home where the need was greatest."},
{q:"Which tribal lands are named in the prophecy Jesus fulfilled?", options:["The land of Zabulon, and the land of Nephthalim","The land of Judah, and the land of Benjamin","The land of Ephraim, and the land of Manasseh","The land of Dan, and the land of Asher"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:15",verse:"The land of Zabulon, and the land of Nephthalim, by the way of the sea, beyond Jordan, Galilee of the Gentiles;", insight:"Zabulon and Nephthalim, Galilee of the Gentiles. The first to fall to Assyria would be the first to see the Light."},
{q:"What did the people which sat in darkness see?", options:["Great light","A star in the east","A pillar of fire","The face of an angel"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:16",verse:"The people which sat in darkness saw great light; and to them which sat in the region and shadow of death light is sprung up.", insight:"Great light. To those sitting in the shadow of death, light sprang up. That is still what Jesus does."},
{q:"What did Jesus begin to preach?", options:["Repent: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand","Believe: for the day of salvation is come","Behold: the Lamb of God is here","Come: the feast is prepared"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:17",verse:"From that time Jesus began to preach, and to say, Repent: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.", insight:"Repent, for the kingdom of heaven is at hand. The same word John preached, now from the King's own lips."},
{q:"Whom did Jesus see casting a net into the sea of Galilee?", options:["Simon called Peter, and Andrew his brother","James and John, the sons of thunder","Philip and Bartholomew","Thomas and Matthew"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:18",verse:"And Jesus, walking by the sea of Galilee, saw two brethren, Simon called Peter, and Andrew his brother, casting a net into the sea: for they were fishers.", insight:"Simon called Peter, and Andrew. He found His first followers at work, not waiting around for a calling."},
{q:"What did Jesus promise to make the fishermen?", options:["Fishers of men","Shepherds of the flock","Builders of the temple","Sowers of the seed"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:19",verse:"And he saith unto them, Follow me, and I will make you fishers of men.", insight:"Fishers of men. He took their old skill and gave it a new sea. God does not waste your past; He redirects it."},
{q:"Who were the other two brethren Jesus called?", options:["James the son of Zebedee, and John his brother","James the son of Alphaeus, and Jude","Philip, and Nathanael","Simon the Zealot, and Judas"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 4:21",verse:"And going on from thence, he saw other two brethren, James the son of Zebedee, and John his brother, in a ship with Zebedee their father, mending their nets; and he called them.", insight:"James and John, mending their nets with their father. They left the ship and their father immediately; some calls cannot wait."}
]},
{n:5, name:"The Sermon on the Mount", seal:{ref:"Matthew 5:16",verse:"Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven."}, facts:["Did you know the Beatitudes turn the world's values upside down? Jesus calls the poor in spirit, the mourners, and the meek blessed, the very people the world pities.","Did you know 'ye are the salt of the earth' and 'ye are the light of the world' were among the first pictures Jesus gave of His followers' mission? Salt preserves and light reveals.","Did you know the sermon was spoken to the disciples, but the multitudes were listening too? Matthew ends the sermon by saying the people were astonished at His teaching."], questions:[
{q:"Where did Jesus go to teach the sermon?", options:["Up into a mountain","Into the temple courts","Down to the seaside","Into a synagogue at Capernaum"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:1",verse:"And seeing the multitudes, he went up into a mountain: and when he was set, his disciples came unto him:", insight:"He went up into a mountain. Like Moses of old, the great Teacher gave the law's true meaning from a height."},
{q:"Who are blessed, and what is theirs?", options:["The poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven","The rich in goods, for theirs is the earth","The strong in arm, for theirs is victory","The wise in counsel, for theirs is honor"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:3",verse:"Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.", insight:"The poor in spirit. The kingdom belongs not to the self-sufficient but to those who know their need."},
{q:"What is promised to them that mourn?", options:["They shall be comforted","They shall be forgotten","They shall be left alone","They shall be made strong"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:4",verse:"Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted.", insight:"They shall be comforted. God does not rush past our grief; He meets us in it with comfort."},
{q:"What shall the meek inherit?", options:["The earth","The kingdom of heaven","Eternal riches","The thrones of kings"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:5",verse:"Blessed are the meek: for they shall inherit the earth.", insight:"The meek shall inherit the earth. Gentleness is not weakness; it is strength surrendered to God, and it wins in the end."},
{q:"What is promised to those who hunger and thirst after righteousness?", options:["They shall be filled","They shall be praised","They shall be made rulers","They shall be given rest"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:6",verse:"Blessed are they which do hunger and thirst after righteousness: for they shall be filled.", insight:"They shall be filled. Hunger for righteousness is the one appetite God promises to fully satisfy."},
{q:"What is promised to the pure in heart?", options:["They shall see God","They shall see angels","They shall see visions","They shall see the temple"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:8",verse:"Blessed are the pure in heart: for they shall see God.", insight:"They shall see God. A clean heart clears the vision; purity is the lens for seeing heaven."},
{q:"What shall the peacemakers be called?", options:["The children of God","The sons of thunder","The friends of kings","The heirs of the earth"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:9",verse:"Blessed are the peacemakers: for they shall be called the children of God.", insight:"The children of God. Peacemakers look like their Father, who reconciled the world to Himself."},
{q:"For whose sake are the persecuted called blessed?", options:["For my sake, says Jesus","For righteousness sake alone","For the prophets sake","For the kingdom's sake"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:11",verse:"Blessed are ye, when men shall revile you, and persecute you, and shall say all manner of evil against you falsely, for my sake.", insight:"For my sake. Suffering counts as blessing when it is for Jesus, not for our own stubbornness."},
{q:"What are Jesus' followers called in verse 13?", options:["The salt of the earth","The bread of life","The water of the well","The oil of gladness"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:13",verse:"Ye are the salt of the earth: but if the salt have lost his savour, wherewith shall it be salted? it is thenceforth good for nothing, but to be cast out, and to be trodden under foot of men.", insight:"The salt of the earth. Salt preserves from rot and gives flavor; that is the quiet work of a faithful life."},
{q:"What are Jesus' followers called in verse 14?", options:["The light of the world","The stars of the sky","The lamps of the temple","The fire of the altar"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:14",verse:"Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid.", insight:"The light of the world. A city on a hill cannot be hid; neither can a life that truly shines."},
{q:"Where do men put a lighted candle?", options:["On a candlestick, not under a bushel","Under a bushel, to keep it safe","Behind the door, out of the wind","In the inner chamber"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:15",verse:"Neither do men light a candle, and put it under a bushel, but on a candlestick; and it giveth light unto all that are in the house.", insight:"On a candlestick. Light is meant to be seen; hiding your faith helps no one find their way."},
{q:"Why should your light shine before men?", options:["That they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven","That they may praise your wisdom","That they may follow your example only","That they may honor your name"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:16",verse:"Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.", insight:"That they may glorify your Father. Good works are signposts, not trophies; they point past us to God."},
{q:"What did Jesus say about the law and the prophets?", options:["I am not come to destroy, but to fulfil","I am come to set them aside","I am come to rewrite them","I am come to hide their meaning"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:17",verse:"Think not that I am come to destroy the law, or the prophets: I am not come to destroy, but to fulfil.", insight:"Not to destroy, but to fulfil. Jesus did not cancel God's law; He completed it and lived it perfectly."},
{q:"What shall in no wise pass from the law?", options:["One jot or one tittle, till all be fulfilled","The sacrifices, till the temple falls","The Sabbaths, till the end of the age","The feasts, till the Messiah comes"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:18",verse:"For verily I say unto you, Till heaven and earth pass, one jot or one tittle shall in no wise pass from the law, till all be fulfilled.", insight:"Not one jot or tittle. God keeps His word down to the smallest stroke; we can trust every letter."},
{q:"What did Jesus say about anger without a cause?", options:["It puts a man in danger of the judgment","It is a small and harmless fault","It is worse than murder itself","It cannot be forgiven"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:22",verse:"But I say unto you, That whosoever is angry with his brother without a cause shall be in danger of the judgment: and whosoever shall say to his brother, Raca, shall be in danger of the council: but whosoever shall say, Thou fool, shall be in danger of hell fire.", insight:"Anger without cause faces judgment. Jesus traces murder back to its root: contempt in the heart."},
{q:"What should you do if you remember your brother has something against you?", options:["Leave your gift before the altar, and first be reconciled to your brother","Offer the gift quickly and then apologize","Pray about it and come back later","Ask the priest to settle it"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:24",verse:"Leave there thy gift before the altar, and go thy way; first be reconciled to thy brother, and then come and offer thy gift.", insight:"First be reconciled. Worship waits while we make peace; God values restored relationships over rituals."},
{q:"What did Jesus say about looking with lust?", options:["It is adultery already in the heart","It is a small temptation, easily dismissed","It is forgiven without repentance","It harms no one"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:28",verse:"But I say unto you, That whosoever looketh on a woman to lust after her hath committed adultery with her already in his heart.", insight:"Adultery in the heart. Jesus judges the inner life, not just the outward act; the battle is won or lost inside."},
{q:"What did Jesus teach about putting away one's wife?", options:["It causes her to commit adultery, saving for the cause of fornication","It is permitted for any reason","It is commanded by the law","It has no consequence before God"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:32",verse:"But I say unto you, That whosoever shall put away his wife, saving for the cause of fornication, causeth her to commit adultery: and whosoever shall marry her that is divorced committeth adultery.", insight:"Marriage is a covenant, not a convenience. Jesus guarded it because God joined it."},
{q:"How should your communication be?", options:["Yea, yea; Nay, nay","Yea, if the priest agrees","Nay, unless you swear by heaven","Yea and nay together, to be safe"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:37",verse:"But let your communication be, Yea, yea; Nay, nay: for whatsoever is more than these cometh of evil.", insight:"Yea, yea; Nay, nay. A plain yes should be enough; honest people do not need oaths to be believed."},
{q:"What did Jesus command concerning enemies?", options:["Love your enemies, and pray for them which despitefully use you","Hate your enemies, as the law allows","Avoid your enemies, and shun them","Curse your enemies, as David did"], a:0, ref:"Matthew 5:44",verse:"But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that hate you, and pray for them which despitefully use you, and persecute you;", insight:"Love your enemies and pray for them. This is the hardest command in the sermon, and the clearest mark of God's children."}
]}
]);
